<sect> swiss projection (Revision 1.2 -- 06/05/98)

<p> In this unit functions to transform coordinates from 
the Bessel ellipsoid to the Swiss military coordinates and the
vice versa are defined. Swiss Military coordinates are
projection coordinates based on the Swiss National Projection
which is a transverse Mercator projection. In addition, their
origin is shifted from (<tt/0, 0/) to (<tt/milx0 = 200'000, 
mily0 = 600'000/). For points in Switzerland this leads to 
positive not overlapping ranges for x and y coordinates.

<p>Only the main transformation functions are descriped in
this documentation. Additional functions which  
correspond to intermediate steps in the transformation
process are available. Consult <tt/swiss.h/ for more details.
Note that normally you don't need these functions.

<sect1> Transformation Functions
<p>

<sect2>ch_elltomil
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int ch_elltomil(double elllat, double elllon, double *milx, double *mily);
</verb></tscreen>

<p> This function calculates the military coordinates <tt/milx/ and <tt/mily/
from the ellipsoidal latitude <tt/elllat/ and longitude <tt/elllon/. The
ellipoidal coordinates must refer to the Swiss Bessel ellipsoid and
have to be passed in radians. The resulting coordinates <tt/milx/ is the 
 south-north component and <tt/mily/ the east-west component. Both are returned
in meters.

<sect2>ch_miltoell
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int ch_miltoell(double milx, double mily, double *elllat, double *elllon);
</verb></tscreen>

<p> This function is the counterpart to <tt/ch_elltomil/. It calculates
the ellipsoidal latitude <tt/elllat/ and  longitude <tt/ellon/ from 
the military coordinates <tt/milx/ and <tt/mily/. Military coordinates
are given in meters. Ellipsoidal coordinates refer to the Swiss Bessel
ellipsoid and are returned in radian. Note that <tt/milx/ corresponds
to the north-south and <tt/mily/ to the east-west component.

<sect2>ch_e2m
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int ch_e2m(double elllat, double elllon, 
	   double *milx, double *mily, 
	   double *scale, double *merconv)
</verb></tscreen>
<p> This function is similar to <tt/ch_elltomil/, but returns to 
additional values: the scale <tt/scale/ and the convergence of the
meridian <tt/merconv/ in radians.

<sect2>ch_m2e
<p>
<tscreen><verb>
int ch_m2e(double milx, double mily,
	   double *elllat, double *elllon,
	   double *scale, double *merconv)
</verb></tscreen>
<p> This function is similar to <tt/ch_miltoell/, but returns to 
additional values: the scale <tt/scale/ and the convergence of the
meridian <tt/merconv/ in radians.

<sect2>ch_magnetic_deviation
<p>

<tscreen><verb>
double ch_magnetic_deviation (const double milx, const double mily, 
                              const double year)
</verb></tscreen>
<p> This function calculates the magnetic deviation using a simple 
polynomial developement. The value is dependant on coordinates and
time given in years. Deviation is returned in radians.
